    "description": "The Feywild operates on a strict lack of metal. The Overgrown Manor is all wood, vines, and magic. Consequently, when the goblin staff found Remi's steam-powered mechanical dog running around, they didn't see a pet—they saw premium scrap metal to help them advance to the 'Guilded Age.' Waluigi finds this entrepreneurial spirit commendable, but stealing from Disaster Inc. is a bad business model.\n\n**Phase 1: The Bathroom Breach**\nToad Lee, displaying a remarkable lack of his usual caution, tracked the dog to the servant's quarters. He barged into a room clearly marked 'OCCUPIED,' discovering a servant on the toilet. Toad Lee politely apologized, backed out, and then immediately breached the correct room across the hall. \n\n**Phase 2: Shield Theft and Gravity**\nThe fight devolved into a chaotic brawl. Gregory, a shockingly competent goblin guard, managed to catch Toad Lee's longsword in his own shield. Hjumpik intervened, using his 'Morning Glory' weapon (a flower bud that blooms into a milky gray steel blade) to stab the goblin. \n\nGregory, unfazed, used his sword to completely wrench Toad Lee's shield out of his hands, mockingly thanking him for the upgrade. Toad Lee attempted a retaliatory acrobatic jump to get behind the goblin, completely misjudged the distance, and plummeted out the window. Waluigi has done this before (usually in Mario Kart), but it is never not embarrassing.\n\n**Phase 3: The Rakasha Intervention**\nToad Lee would have plummeted to the library below, but Azure (the incredibly intoxicated Rakasha) manifested a giant, glowing blue ghost-hand and snatched him out of the air. She hauled him back inside, then casually walked over an unconscious staff member (producing a distinct squish noise) and grabbed the mechanical dog.\n\nHjumpik finished the fight by perfectly striking Gregory's stolen shield with his warhammer, knocking it out of the goblin's hands. Hjumpik then de-escalated the situation, offering Gregory a truce. Toad Lee immediately looted Gregory's pockets while Hjumpik wasn't looking. Flawless teamwork.",
