    "summary": "Waluigi hates musicals. He especially hates musicals where the chorus tries to strangle you. Markop's rescue team was ambushed in a petrified hedge maze by the 'Mazebound'—grey-skinned ghouls who sing theatrical patter-songs while ripping you apart. The party survived, but Dan was dragged away into the hedges. Waluigi considers this the most undignified battle of the campaign.",
    "description": "After the Shadow Anchor shattered, the estate's grounds became even more hostile. Markop, leading Remi, Dan, Salam, and Eager, ventured into the estate's hedge maze looking for Archie. Instead of Archie, they found the Mazebound.\n\n**The Ambush**\nThe Mazebound are hunched, snub-nosed humanoids with glowing white eyes and sharp nails. But their physical threat is secondary to their psychological warfare: they sing. They leaped out of the hedges doing 'jazz hands' and immediately launched into a rhyming chorus: 'Welcome to the grove, welcome to the gray! You'll never find the fountain so you might as well stay!'\n\nWaluigi finds this deeply offensive. If you are going to taunt your enemies, do it with a sharp laugh or a magnificent monologue. Do not do a choreographed routine in a hedge maze.\n\n**The Choreographed Violence**\nThe fight was chaotic. The Mazebound encircled the party, specifically targeting their weaknesses while singing a rapid patter-song: 'Check the Turtle! Big and loud! Check the Archer! Check the Whip! Check the Toads—one blue, one green? Or is he purple? Is he mean?'\n\nMarkop, proving his absolute pragmatism, ignored the music and coated his sword in an 'undead remedy.' When a Mazebound lunged, Markop struck, melting the creature's grey skin off its bones. Remi, still suffering from blood loss, tried to stab a Mazebound, but her dagger had no effect on its thick skin. The creature mocked her, attempting to give her a 'goodbye kiss' before Remi dodged and Salam provided covering fire.\n\n**The Abduction of Dan**\nThe tragedy of this skirmish was Dan. Or rather, the 'Parallel Dan'. While Markop was bashing heads and Eager was tripping ghouls with his whip, the Mazebound swarmed Dan. They dragged him backward into the impenetrable petrified hedges. \n\nBowser arrived moments later, entirely missing the musical number, and completely incinerated a section of the maze with his fire breath. But it was too late. Dan was gone, and the Mazebound retreated into the shadows, leaving only the echo of their terrible singing.",
    "aftermath": "The party was forced to press forward without Dan, deeply unnerved by the encounter. They eventually found the groundskeeper's cottage and discovered Archie's discarded pouch and watch, proving Archie had survived but was on the run. Waluigi hopes he never has to fight the Mazebound. Waluigi refuses to participate in a duet with a zombie.",
