    "summary": "General Ironhand issued Order 120 to execute all Toad prisoners. Speaker L responded by proving he had already rigged the entire fortress to explode. Using peppermint gas, mini-mushrooms baked into bread crusts, and a decoy Speaker L painted green, 158 Toads broke out of the Legion's most secure facility. Waluigi has never respected Speaker L more. It was a masterclass in chaotic logistics.",
    "description": "Waluigi must correct the historical record: The Iron Legion thought they were conducting a purge. Speaker L was conducting a symphony of sabotage.\n\n**Phase 1: The Bread Code and the Green Fog**\nSpeaker L, operating through a hacked terminal, synchronized a flawless prison break. Kitchen sympathizers smuggled 'Mini-Mushrooms' inside the prisoners' hardtack rations. At the ringing of the third bell, the laundry vents began spewing a custom-synthesized peppermint gas designed specifically to choke Imperial lungs while leaving Toads unharmed. \n\n**Phase 2: The Miniature Escape**\nAs the guards choked, the prisoners consumed the Mini-Mushrooms, shrinking to a fraction of their size to slip out of their cuffs and down the floor drains. They followed paths of bioluminescent moss planted weeks in advance by Noki smugglers. It was an underground highway of tiny, angry amphibians.\n\n**Phase 3: Boiler Sabotage and Extraction**\nToads jammed the boiler pressure valves with discarded Imperial service medals—a touch of poetic irony that Waluigi deeply appreciates. The resulting steam explosion blew out the east wall, blinding the Legion's drones and snipers. The prisoners poured out, utilizing makeshift ziplines made of bedsheets, and dove off a 50-foot cliff into the river where Noki submersibles were waiting.\n\n**The Aftermath:**\nGeneral Ironhand's 'Order 120' was meant to erase a problem. Instead, it exposed the Iron Legion as hollow. They lost 158 prisoners, their base was humiliated, and they discovered their 'Speaker L' captive was just a decoy dyed green. However, Bones was unmasked and stabbed by Ironhand during the chaos, leaving his fate uncertain. Waluigi takes notes: never put Waluigi in a cell, because Waluigi will turn the plumbing into a weapon. WAH!",
    "aftermath": "The myth of the Iron Legion's invincibility was shattered. The refugees fled toward the Whispering Caves and eventually the Mushroom Kingdom borders. The Legion is now out for blood, and Speaker L has solidified his position as a terrifyingly competent tactical mastermind.",
