    "summary": "The Siege of Toad Town is less a single battle and more an ongoing catastrophe. When Princess Peach vanished, the capital became contested ground between Peach Loyalists, Liberators, and Fawful's forces. The fighting has destroyed the central fountain, burned the market district, partially collapsed Peach's Castle, and turned a vibrant city into a three-way war zone. Waluigi remembers Toad Town's tennis courts. Those courts are rubble now.",
    "description": "Waluigi cannot write about the Siege of Toad Town as a single battle because it ISN'T a single battle. It's an ongoing disaster that has been grinding for months.\n\n## The Collapse of Order\n\nWhen Princess Peach vanished, Toad Town's stability evaporated overnight. The Toad Council attempted to maintain governance, but their authority depended on Peach's legitimacy. Without her, factions that had been suppressed or marginalized saw opportunity.\n\nThe Peach Loyalists emerged from the castle garrison, claiming to defend the throne. Their definition of 'defense' expanded rapidly to include controlling the city, suppressing dissent, and establishing what would become Captain Toadette's authoritarian apparatus.\n\nResistance formed in the outer districts—neighborhoods where Loyalist influence was weaker. What became the Liberated Toads started as mutual aid networks that evolved into armed resistance.\n\nFawful's forces entered from the east, seizing industrial districts before anyone could organize defense. His mechanical troops attacked everyone equally, turning political crisis into three-way war.\n\n## The Destruction\n\nToad Town has been destroyed piece by piece:\n\n- **The Central Fountain** — Shelled in the first week during Loyalist artillery targeting Liberator positions\n- **The Market District** — Burned during street fighting when alchemical supplies ignited\n- **Peach's Castle** — Besieged, relieved, besieged again, partially collapsed from undermining\n- **Residential Districts** — Evacuated, looted, repurposed as military positions\n- **The Pipe Network** — Partially functional but dangerous, some routes sabotaged\n\nThe city Waluigi remembers—colorful, vibrant, full of Toads who smiled at strangers—no longer exists. The geography remains. The spirit is gone.\n\n## Current Status\n\nControl changes constantly. Loyalists hold the castle ruins and northern approaches. Fawful maintains eastern industrial positions. Liberators control scattered pockets. Combat is constant—not organized battles but grinding urban attrition.\n\nCivilians who could flee have fled. Those remaining survive through improvisation, trading, and hoping whichever faction controls their block this week shows mercy.\n\nInfrastructure has collapsed. Water is sporadic. Power fails unpredictably. The systems that made urban life possible have broken down, and nobody has resources to fix them while fighting continues.\n\n## Waluigi's Memory\n\nWaluigi competed in Toad Town. Tennis tournaments near the eastern gate. Kart races through streets while crowds cheered. Dance competitions in the central square.\n\nThose memories belong to a different world now. The courts are rubble. The streets are combat zones. The square is a crater.\n\nWaluigi doesn't know if Toad Town can be rebuilt. The physical damage might be repairable given decades and resources. The loss of community, culture, trust? Those don't rebuild easily.\n\nSomeday there might be tennis courts again. Waluigi has to believe that, or what's the point?\n\nWAH.",
    "aftermath": "The siege continues. Toad Town remains contested ground. Refugees scatter across the region. The city that was the Mushroom Kingdom's heart has become its wound.",
