    "casualties": {
      "attackers": "One imp crushed by Bowser",
      "defenders": "Remi petrified; one bloody toadburt 'erased' by the Archivist"
    },
    "summary": "What began as a search for Archie became a coordinated trap. Imps led Remi to a locked room. The Archivist threatened to kill her friends with transformed monsters. Bowser retreated to save lives. Guards blocked every exit except one. That exit led to a medusa's workshop. Remi is now stone. The Oracle's Deck—prophecy cards of significant power—are with her or nearby. Rescue is urgent. Time may be limited.",
    "description": "Waluigi documents this event with the urgency it deserves. Remi is PETRIFIED. This is not a metaphor for being scared. She has been turned to STONE by a medusa's gaze and is currently a statue in a workshop full of statues.\n\n## Sequence of Events\n\n### Day 1: The Setup\n\nThe Onyx Hand guards had been behaving strangely around Remi:\n\n**The 'Cure':** Guards claimed they would cure Remi of 'purpleeyetus'—the toads were skeptical, but Remi trusted them because 'they said they were going to help.'\n\n**The Ring:** A guard delivered a letter 'from your vampire friends' containing a 'friendship ring.' The letter used handwriting Remi recognized from a guest book. The ring leaked faint smoke. Remi kept it.\n\n**The Anklet:** When Remi declined a second ring, guards offered a 'friendship anklet.' Remi declined due to no accompanying letter. The guards were PERSISTENT.\n\n**The 'Accident':** A guard 'tripped' into Remi, cutting her eye with a gash—just as Markop was asking to examine her eyes. Convenient timing.\n\n**Strategic Repositioning:** Guards moved into blocking positions: 5 at the corner door, 5 cornering toads, 5 blocking Bowser, Markop, and Remi. Battle seemed imminent.\n\n**Marcus Ashford's Intervention:** The Onyx Hand representative appeared, de-escalated the situation, gave Remi a potion that turned her eyes blue (curing the purple condition), and pickpocketed a letter from Bowser.\n\n### Day 2: The Trap Springs\n\nRemi's ring leaked black smoke. Guards claimed it needed 'recharging' due to 'leaking entropy.'\n\nMarkop completed a ritual revealing:\n- The ring contained necromancy magic\n- Another ring in Remi's pocket contained destructive magic\n- Magical signatures in the walls suggested surveillance\n\nThe toads observed Marcus steal Bowser's paper but said nothing until later—triggering confrontation when Bowser noticed his missing paperwork.\n\nMarcus taunted everyone with rhyming verse, read part of Bowser's letter aloud, and mocked the 'three-eyed failure' (Archie), the 'dwarf and toads,' and Bowser's lost throne.\n\nThe group decided to find Archie at the airship. Marcus claimed Archie's 'eyes rolled so far back he lost the plot.'\n\n### The Library Trap\n\nRemi headed downstairs to the library. Imps claimed they had 'found Archie' and led her to a room.\n\nThe room was locked.\n\nBowser shouted 'REMI NO' and busted down the door. He grabbed an imp and crushed it—blood emerged, confirming they were real creatures. He threw the corpse to a flower plant.\n\nRemi entered the Archivist's room. The door locked behind her.\n\nThe Archivist snapped his fingers and declared:\n- She was 'free to go'\n- Her friends would 'die at the hands of imps'\n- He had 'erased' a bloody toadburt found in the room\n- He told 'FNG' to leave\n\nBowser saw the imps transform into giants, demons, and monsters. Overwhelming force.\n\nThe Archivist smiled as he 'led Remi to the exit door.'\n\nBowser thought: 'I don't want these people to die. Hjumpik wouldn't like this.' He left the grand entrance open and retreated—allowing others to escape the transformed creatures.\n\n### The Workshop\n\nRemi found only one way forward. Guards blocked every door. She was alone.\n\nOne door remained: the workshop.\n\nShe entered.\n\nLyranth waited—a medusa with marble-pale skin covered in vibrant paint, crown of snakes swaying, surrounded by her partially-completed masterpieces. Statues of stunning artistry. Statues that were once people.\n\nLyranth glared at Remi.\n\nShe said: 'Smile.'\n\nRemi turned to stone.\n\n## Critical Assets at Risk\n\n**The Oracle's Deck:** Remi possesses magical tarot cards that predict the future—cards that showed Hjumpik navigating the Maze of Time, Markop wrestling the Arachnid Matriarch, and Lady Aurelian Corvinarus in the Feywild. These cards are significant prophetic artifacts.\n\n- Are they petrified with Remi?\n- Did they fall when she transformed?\n- Can they function while their bearer is stone?\n\n**Intelligence:** Remi gathered significant information throughout the estate—Ryan's diary, guard patterns, power dynamics. This intelligence is now inaccessible.\n\n**The Rings:** Remi possessed at least two magical rings—one necromantic, one destructive. These artifacts are now with her statue.\n\n## Rescue Parameters\n\nMedusa petrification has varying reversibility:\n\n**Time Sensitivity:** Some petrification becomes permanent after hours or days. Immediate action may be critical.\n\n**Reversal Methods:** Specific spells, alchemical agents, or medusa-specific countermeasures might reverse the transformation.\n\n**Lyranth's Cooperation:** The medusa herself might be able to reverse her work—if persuaded, threatened, or bargained with.\n\n**Estate Resources:** The Shadow Estate's infirmary or other facilities might possess reversal capabilities—though trusting estate resources seems inadvisable given who orchestrated the trap.\n\n## Rescue Challenges\n\n**Location Unknown:** Bowser, Markop, and the toads fled transformed monsters. They may not know Remi entered the workshop. They may not know she's petrified.\n\n**The Archivist:** The orchestrator remains active, commands transformed creatures, and has demonstrated willingness to 'erase' people.\n\n**Lyranth:** Even if rescuers reach the workshop, they face a medusa. Looking at her means petrification. Fighting her requires not looking. This is difficult.\n\n**Succession Crisis:** The broader estate remains in chaos. Vivian hunts through corridors. Guards have divided loyalties. Resources are contested.\n\n## Waluigi's Assessment\n\nThis was not random violence. This was a COORDINATED TRAP:\n\n1. Isolate Remi from allies\n2. Threaten allies with overwhelming force to ensure separation\n3. Block all exits except one\n4. Funnel victim to Lyranth\n5. Petrify\n\nThe Archivist orchestrated this. Lyranth executed it. The guards facilitated it. Someone wanted Remi neutralized specifically—possibly for the Oracle's Deck, possibly for her gathered intelligence, possibly for reasons not yet apparent.\n\nRescue is URGENT. Waluigi cannot help directly from the Feywild. The toads, Bowser, and Markop must realize Remi is missing, deduce her location, and mount a rescue operation against a medusa in a vampire estate during a succession crisis while transformed monsters roam the corridors.\n\nThe odds are not good. But Disaster Inc. has survived worse odds. Waluigi has to believe they'll find a way.\n\nWAH.",
    "aftermath": "Remi remains petrified. Her allies are scattered, potentially unaware of her fate. The Archivist's trap succeeded. Lyranth has a new potential sculpture. Time is unknown but likely limited.",
