    "casualties": {
      "attackers": "Kamek (power stripped, imprisoned), Corrupted Koopa forces (eradicated)",
      "defenders": "38 Resistance members KIA (including Demolitions Bob-omb and the Heroic Shy Guy), The entire Valley ecosystem"
    },
    "summary": "While Bowser was away, Kamek decided to play god. He dug under the castle and awakened the Primordial Wyrm—a cosmic parasite older than the stars that the Koopa Dynasty was originally founded to keep locked up. A ragtag resistance of Goombas, Shy Guys, and Hammer Bros had to blow up seven anchor crystals to re-seal the beast. Waluigi respects the sheer, apocalyptic ambition of Kamek, but it was a terrible real estate decision.",
    "description": "Waluigi must clarify the true nature of the Koopa Kingdom. Bowser’s ancestors were not just tyrants who liked lava; they were *wardens*. Their castle was built as a lid on a metaphysical prison holding the Primordial Wyrm, a reality-eating entity. Kamek, believing he could harness this power to defeat the Iron Legion and Mario, reversed the polarity of the prison seals.\n\n**The Coup and the Corruption**\nDeclaring himself the 'Regent Sorcerer,' Kamek began feeding loyal troops to the Wyrm, turning them into purple-veined, hollowed-out husks. The valley sky turned purple, and the earth vibrated with the creature's hunger. \n\n**The Working-Class Resistance**\nWith Bowser weeks away in the Midlands, the kingdom was saved not by royalty, but by the construction crew. A Koopa Foreman, a Hammer Bro Sergeant, a Demolitions Bob-omb, and a deeply traumatized Shy Guy formed the 'Koopa Resistance.' They discovered the original blueprints for the seven seals holding the Wyrm. \n\n**The Seven Seals**\nIn a desperate, multi-day campaign, the Resistance struck the anchors. The final battle took place at the Volcanic Shrine. Kamek, now thirty feet tall and warping reality, erased entire squads from existence. The detonator broke, forcing the Demolitions Bob-omb to sacrifice himself to shatter the final crystal. The Shy Guy walked directly into the Wyrm's light to detonate another anchor from the inside. \n\nWith the anchors destroyed, the prison reformed, dragging the Wyrm—and Kamek's borrowed power—back into the earth.",
    "aftermath": "Bowser returned to find his valley in ruins, but his kingdom saved by the grunts he usually ignores. He promoted the Hammer Bro to General and sentenced Kamek to eternal imprisonment in the very pit he opened. The Koopa Troop is battered, but unified by trauma. Waluigi sheds a single tear for the Bob-omb. What a way to go.",
